WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.342
How many people are in the Delish team?

2
00:00:03.342 --> 00:00:07.790
In this lesson, you will learn to count rows in a filtered table with

3
00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:12.238
COUNTX and FILTER, give the measure a clear name, and add it to your

4
00:00:12.238 --> 00:00:13.509
report with a title.

5
00:00:13.509 --> 00:00:14.780
Let's count a team!

6
00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.702
Here is our measure from before, Bars Category.

7
00:00:19.702 --> 00:00:23.080
Now I create a new measure called Delish Category.

8
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.337
I type COUNTX.

9
00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:39.990
COUNTX needs a table and an expression.

10
00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:44.160
For the table, I use FILTER on the Sales Person table.

11
00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:56.964
The condition:

12
00:00:56.964 --> 00:00:59.637
Sales Person, Team, equals Delish, in quotes.

13
00:00:59.637 --> 00:01:02.692
Then a comma, and the expression to count:

14
00:01:02.692 --> 00:01:04.220
one, for each row.

15
00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:20.596
Press Enter, and add the measure to a card. The answer: seven.

16
00:01:20.596 --> 00:01:23.160
Seven salespeople belong to the Delish team.

17
00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.210
The name Delish Category is not quite right.

18
00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:43.844
It counts a team, not a category.

19
00:01:43.844 --> 00:01:46.479
So I rename the measure Delish Team.

20
00:01:46.479 --> 00:01:48.360
Clear names save confusion later.

21
00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.480
I add a text box title:

22
00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:40.000
COUNTX, and a subtitle:

23
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.520
Number of Delish Team.

24
00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.582
Now the page has four groups:

25
00:02:58.582 --> 00:03:01.361
COUNT, DISTINCTCOUNT, COUNTROWS with FILTER, and COUNTX.

26
00:03:01.361 --> 00:03:04.140
Each one counts in its own way.

27
00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.037
Next, I start a new measure.

28
00:03:16.037 --> 00:03:18.180
Keep building, one measure at a time!

